re.","contributions":[{"graphFunctionRef":"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/uat@5","contribution":"Carry out a read-only, independent assessment of the complete original basic-cli outcome. The selected subject is the current C2 measurement b609386b…. Read these exact current files:\n- candidate generated/hello-world.mjs (fe8f4080…);\n- the original source (ce602ce2…), the oracle rubric (028073e4…) and the witness contract (f97359de…);\n- both supplied tests (8b55bf3f… and 5449c227…);\n- the four authored assets as they exist now: conformance a74a75b6…, implementation design 801f3ab5…, test design a9bf5d5f… and plan ed573966….\n\nReturn a verdict for each of the seven obligations, and keep any unmet or indeterminate criteria.\n\n(1) Conformance\n- Does the content cover Intent, Product boundary, source-grounded requirements REQ-01..14 and completion criteria AC-01..15?\n- Are conflicts C1..C8 and unknowns U1..U5 handled faithfully?\n- Do the proposed non-material frame dispositions (Design Component, Install) hold?\n\n(2) Implementation design\n- Is it realizable and faithful to the original source and to the conformance asset?\n- Does it name the correct source surface and the component and UAT verification surfaces?\n- Does it match the actual CLI bytes?\n\n(3) Test design\n- Does it preserve status 0 and exact stdout \"Hello, world!\\n\"?\n- Is it accurate about the actual supplied verifiers and their limits (stderr, arguments/stdin, hangs, Node version)?\n- Do the mechanically identical component and UAT tests satisfy the distinct component-stage and user-outcome-stage meanings? This is an open judgment; decide it explicitly.\n\n(4) Execution plan\n- Does it have command \"node\"; the exact args; expectedTestPassCount ≥ 2; expectedStdoutMatch containing \"fail 0\" with no pass count pinned; and assertedReturnValue \"Hello, world!\"?\n- Judge the C4 resolution (fixedCommands alongside the top-level command) and the C5 resolution (the newline carried in